    basic: 'Prioritize the Red Ace! It is the single most valuable card (20 points). Since it can only be captured by a 9, never play your Red 9 unless you are sure you can snatch the Red Ace or if the Ace is already gone.',
    intermediate: "The 'Setup' Discard: If you have a Black 4 and a Red 4, play the Black 4 to the table if there is a 6 you want. If you don't capture it immediately, you might lure your opponent into playing an 8, which you can then take with a different card.",
    advanced: "Table Clearing (Clean): In many Indonesian house rules, clearing the table entirely (taking the last cards) gives a huge point bonus. Manage your 10-sum pairs to ensure you are the last one with a 'killing' move.",
